{
  "schema": "headroom.circuit.v1",
  "id": "vox-ac15-handwired",
  "version": 1,
  "name": "Vox AC15 Handwired",
  "description": "Vox AC-15 (factory drawing No. V-1-5, 'Vox AC-15 Amplifier'), both channels. Normal: EF86 pentode -> R29 500k volume -> C27 into V5A. Vib/Trem: V1 ECC83 first stage and split-load driver feeding the HI and LO RC paths; V4 ECC82 modulator pair (common plate node, shared 1.5k cathode) blending them under the Vibravox's antiphase LFO; the 5 x 0.005 uF / 1 MOhm output ladder; R30 500k volume -> C28 into V5B. V5 ECC83 long-tailed pair mixing the two channels (1.2k shared cathode, 47k tail, 1M grid returns to the tail node, 100k plates from the R43 22k / C26 8 uF node) -> C32 / C33 -> TOP CUT 250k + 0.005 across the EL84 grids -> 2 x EL84 cathode bias -> T2 (8 Ohm tap) -> 12-inch speaker. Vibravox: V6 ECC83 phase-shift oscillator (3 x 0.01 uF, R65 / R68 1 MOhm on the footswitch return, SW5 speed switch R64 / R66 / R67) and LFO phase splitter with the R46 depth preset; SW4 tremolo; SW6 footswitch. The Input control picks the jack the guitar goes into: Normal (default), Vib-Trem (the channel the Vibravox acts on) or both jumpered. Supply: EZ81 (GZ34 card) -> 32 uF reservoir (325 V) -> 10-20 H choke -> the +315 V node (OT centre tap, screens); R7 22k -> the vib/trem 210 V node; R43 22k -> V5. EL84 screens through R62 / R63 100 Ohm and the OT centre tap from the +315 V node after the choke, cathodes on R60 130 Ohm / C39 50 uF, as drawn.",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "S. Luckey, Vox AC-15 (V-1-5 reproduced, plus the vibrato channel and Vibravox redrawn with measured voltages; note 2: SW5 speed switch R64 / R66 / R67)",
      "url": "https://sluckeyamps.com/VAC15/Vox_AC15.pdf"
    },
    {
      "title": "Vox AC-15 Amplifier, factory schematic No. V-1-5 (all values, the 315 V / 210 V / 90 V supply nodes, EZ81, 2 x EL84 6BQ5, T2 15/8 Ohm, SW3 BRILLIANCE, SW4 TREMOLO, SW5 VIB/TREM, SW2 voltage selector)",
      "url": "https://el34world.com/charts/Schematics/files/Vox/Vox_AC15.pdf"
    },
    {
      "title": "Koren-form triode/beam-tetrode cards from the engine library (12AX7, EL84, GZ34) - the same cards the 5E3 netlist uses",
      "url": "app/src/circuit/library/EmbeddedLibrary.hpp"
    }
  ],
  "minRate": 176400,
  "lte": {"start": "bdf2", "tol": 8},
  "io": {
    "input": "in",
    "output": "spk",
    "inputVoltsPerFS": 1.0,
    "outputVoltsPerFS": 184.36,
    "note": "outputVoltsPerFS 20 -> 94.63 (2026-11-10): keeps the shipped level within 1 dB of the previous release after the refitted valve cards and the EF86 stage rewired to the factory drawing (DI level +13.50 dB at the same scale). 94.63 -> 116.16 (2026-11-10): the Vibravox rebuild removed the old fabricated vibrato-channel join (C25 33 nF from the mixer plate into V5B's grid), which had attenuated the normal channel; DI level +2.51 dB clean (riff at 0.05 V peak) / +1.04 dB driven (0.5 V peak) at the same scale, retuned to +0.73 / -0.74 dB. 116.16 -> 130.17 (2026-11-10): V5 rebuilt to the drawing's long-tailed pair; DI level vs the release before today +1.79 dB clean / +0.19 dB driven at 116.16, retuned to +0.80 / -0.80 dB. 130.17 -> 184.36 (2026-11-10): Tone Cut direction fixed (0 = no cut) and the EL84 screens / OT centre tap rebuilt to the drawing (+315 V after the choke, HT refitted to the drawing's 325 / 315 V); DI level vs the release before today +3.87 dB clean / +2.18 dB driven at 130.17, retuned to +0.85 / -0.85 dB"
  },
